From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tyn <tyn@localhost>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:33:54 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] tyn: recover from opcodes whose group has no table for the
 instruction set

Upstreamable generic engine fix.

OpcodeTableTitleOnly (group 0x20) and OpcodeTableGraph3D (group 0x02) are
null for most instruction sets; a script reaching such an opcode called a
null pointer. Treat the group as unknown instead and take the existing
"Thread CRASH! Unknown opcode. Attempting recovery" path. Instruction sets
that have the table are unaffected.

diff --git a/src/vm/vm.cpp b/src/vm/vm.cpp
index e0ec54450ff736c1655f6aebbb533dc4fb2201c8..ffdf59417576186b7e3af32b72cdc0f88a7a127e 100644
--- a/src/vm/vm.cpp
+++ b/src/vm/vm.cpp
@@ -505,11 +505,11 @@ void RunThread(Sc3VmThread* thread, float dt) {
              "{:d}\n",
              scriptIp, thread->Id, opcodeGrp1, opcode, thread->ScriptBufferId);
 
-      if (opcodeGrp1 == 0x20) {
+      if (opcodeGrp1 == 0x20 && OpcodeTableTitleOnly) {
         OpcodeTableTitleOnly[opcode](thread, dt);
       } else if (opcodeGrp1 == 0x10) {
         OpcodeTableUser1[opcode](thread, dt);
-      } else if (opcodeGrp1 == 0x02) {
+      } else if (opcodeGrp1 == 0x02 && OpcodeTableGraph3D) {
         OpcodeTableGraph3D[opcode](thread, dt);
       } else if (opcodeGrp1 == 0x01) {
         OpcodeTableGraph[opcode](thread, dt);
